    <section class="csm-card csm-settings-transfer" aria-labelledby="csm-transfer-settings-title"><div class="csm-panel-body">
        <h2 id="csm-transfer-settings-title">Transfer preferences</h2>
        <p class="csm-note"><label for="csm-transport">Transfer method</label> <select id="csm-transport" aria-describedby="csm-transport-help"><option value="stream" <?php selected($transfer_defaults['transport'], 'stream'); ?>>Automatic (recommended)</option><option value="chunks" <?php selected($transfer_defaults['transport'], 'chunks'); ?>>512 KB chunks</option></select> <span id="csm-transport-help">Continuous downloads, 16 MiB uploads. Both methods resume.</span></p>
        <p class="csm-note"><label><input type="checkbox" id="csm-file-verify" <?php checked($transfer_defaults['file_verify']); ?>> Recalculate plugin and theme checksums</label> — for files changed without a metadata change. Otherwise, cached checksums are used.</p>
        <p id="csm-transfer-settings-status" class="csm-inline-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
        <h3>Exclusions</h3>
        <p class="csm-note">Always excluded: <code>node_modules</code>, <code>.git</code>, <code>.gitignore</code>, and environment files (<code>.env</code>, <code>.env.*</code>, <code>*.env</code>). Existing destination copies are kept. Git folders are skipped unless explicitly included.</p>
    </div></section>
        <details class="csm-requirements"><summary>Connection requirements &amp; transfer limits</summary><p>Both sites need this plugin and 64-bit PHP 8.1+, cURL, writable private temporary storage, and writable selected destination files. Production connections require verified HTTPS. Endpoint: <code>?trickle=…</code>; requests use signed <code>X-CSM-*</code> headers.</p><p>Trickle supports single sites with InnoDB, MEMORY and MyISAM tables. Related foreign-key tables must be selected together. Non-InnoDB snapshots require source LOCK TABLES permission. It transfers selected plugins, themes, tables and media, not WordPress core or wp-config.php. Destination URLs, Trickle credentials, and cron schedule are preserved. Plugin activation follows the source unless disabled. Database transfers can replace user accounts and other integration settings; keep destination login access and backups available.</p><p>Transfers use retained source snapshots with resumable streaming or 512 KB chunks. Retry resumes at the destination checkpoint. Building the source stream and final staging can still hit hosting time limits; both sites need temporary disk space. Transfers stage privately and validate checksums before applying. The three most recent backups are kept on the destination. Rollback restores the earlier data and will overwrite changes made after applying.</p></details>
    </section>
